This project implements the "LLM Wiki" pattern proposed by Andrej Karpathy
(https://x.com/karpathy/status/2039805659525644595).

It is an independent, local-first implementation built on Marimo + SQLite/FTS5.
It is not a fork or a port of an existing application: the design and the large
majority of the code are original to this project, including the chat agent, the
ingestion-pipeline orchestration, wiki generation, the lint and repair
subsystems, the ingestion trace, the multi-wiki registry, and the Marimo apps.


Attribution
-----------

A small, foundational slice of the document-ingestion and indexing layer was
reused from the open-source "LLM Wiki" project by Lucas Astorian
(https://github.com/lucasastorian/llmwiki), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. That project is a hosted web application (FastAPI + Supabase + a web
frontend) with a different architecture and feature set; only the following
low-level, framework-agnostic pieces were carried over into this codebase:

  * base/domain/ingestion/pdf_extract.py — PDF-to-markdown extraction.
      Closely based on the upstream module; largely unchanged apart from a
      deferred import and an updated docstring.

  * base/domain/ingestion/chunker.py  — text chunking
  * base/domain/tools/references.py   — citation / cross-reference parsing
  * database/sqlite_schema.sql        — SQLite schema
      Partially derived from the upstream equivalents, then modified and
      extended for this project.

Everything not listed above was written for this project.
